course: dictionary
lesson: 1470
title: Catalytic: speeding things up
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Catalytic is an adjective, and it comes from the noun catalyst. A catalyst is a substance that speeds up a chemical reaction without being used up at the end. So something catalytic is working as a catalyst, or causing important changes to happen.
explain: Read the clues around the word. «A catalytic converter changes some poisonous gases into less harmful ones.» A converter changes things, so the word tells you it helps a change happen. Try your meaning in the sentence: a converter that helps change gases still makes sense.
explain: The word has two meanings. In science it is about reactions, like enzymes in your body, which speed up reactions. In everyday life it describes a change that matters a lot, such as a catalytic role in a team. «Platinum is used in car parts called catalytic converters that clean exhaust fumes.» The parts clean the fumes, and the platinum helps this happen.
fact: Catalyst is a noun; catalytic is the adjective.
fact: A catalyst speeds up a chemical reaction without being used up.
fact: «Catalytic» means working as a catalyst, or causing important changes.
fact: A «catalytic converter» changes some poisonous gases into less harmful ones in a car's exhaust.
fact: Enzymes in the body work like catalysts, speeding up reactions.
exercise: «A catalytic converter changes some poisonous gases into less harmful ones.» What does a catalytic converter do? | *It changes harmful gases into less harmful ones | It makes the car quieter on hills | It makes the car go faster | It stores water for the engine
exercise: What does a catalyst do in a chemical reaction? | It makes the reaction slower | *It speeds the reaction up without being used up | It is always made of water | It stops the reaction for good
exercise: «Platinum is rarer than gold and is used in car parts called catalytic converters.» Find and copy the word that describes the converters. | exhaust | rarer | *catalytic | platinum
test: Someone says, «Her catalytic role in the team made the project succeed.» What does catalytic suggest? | *Causing an important change | Being very slow and careless | Something made of platinum | Sitting quietly in the corner
test: Catalyst is what kind of word? | An adjective only | A verb meaning to burn | *A noun | A question word
exam: Which sentence uses catalytic correctly? | The cake was catalytic and tasted of soap | *The new teacher had a catalytic effect, and the class started working together for the first time | Catalytic means sleeping quietly at night | The dog was catalytic because it was grey
